ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  With the advent of the spring season, Hokuto prepared to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He journeyed to Cherrywood.
  During early summer, Hokuto could not cast Resurrection on Ningarl because 
Ningarl was still alive.  Instead, Hokuto practiced hard for months and his 
skill in Thievery increased.

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Mountain province of St 
Helens, held by Hokuto.  St Helens was overrun by Uga-Buga Makumb's host.  
Uga-Buga Makumb leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 3 Legion, 2 Chariots, 3 
Dragons and 2 Trolls.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  Hokuto travelled to 
Amberleaf.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Amberleaf, a 
Forest area owned by Hokuto.  Teleko (#72)'s armies took possession of 
Amberleaf practically uncontested.  Teleko leads approximately 4 Eagles and 1
Trolls.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Kilkenny, a 
Plain area owned by Hokuto.  Kilkenny was overrun and occupied by 
Constantine (#49)'s host.  Constantine leads approximately 1 Phalanx, 3 
Chariots, 1 Camel Corps and 1 Were-Beasts.
  With the advent of the fall season Hokuto cast a Flood spell and Amberleaf 
was magically flooded.
  During early winter, Hokuto could not recruit Axemen and Axemen in 
Amberleaf because Hokuto does not own that province, and mercenaries weren't 
available.  So, Hokuto discovered nothing worthy of note in his sagely 
experiments.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Hokuto for this year.

  Mugai (#3) Treated with Hokuto, but Hokuto did not react favorably to his 
amicable overtures.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings will see the 
wisdom of Treating.


  Here is the financial report for Hokuto's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Hokuto was left with 16 gold in 
the treasury.


